    panelD = {
      display = "Intact Elysium",
      isOutdoors = false,
      isDaytime = false,
      weather = {},
      locationAudio = "quietIndoor",
      url = ""
    },
    blindfoldURL = "At a barricaded nighttime avenue, Lucien strides beside a burning automobile while a vast illusion of disciplined Camarilla reinforcements appears across the rooftops and at the far end of the street. The phantom soldiers are fully rendered and slightly brighter and more saturated than reality, every silhouette thinly limned by violet-purple smoke; the space inside the smoky contours contains the coherent false army rather than empty fog. They aim weapons and advance with impossible confidence, forcing a larger Anarch group to turn, scatter, and redeploy while the real handful of Camarilla survivors escapes through a side street. Lucien directs the retreat with a charismatic theatrical gesture and defiant half-smirk as the false army's outer ranks begin unraveling into purple vapor against searchlit clouds.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow, neutral black cross-shaped gutter to keep the four scenes visually separate; do not let figures, smoke, fire, architecture, or lighting cross between quads. Do not place letters, captions, borders around individual quads, logos, watermarks, or other readable text in the image.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs to the generation call; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black and charcoal, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet and metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, locations, symbols, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/lord-lucien.webp` as the exact identity reference for Lord Lucien; preserve his facial structure, blond curls, slim build, apparent age, and identity while dressing him in smoke-marked 1944 evening clothes or a tailored wartime overcoat. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/composition/overlay_explode_image_lordLucien.png` only as a structural reference for Chimerstry revealing coherent illusionary imagery; do not copy its red color, modern costume, seated composition, surrounding portraits, or Toronto imagery.\n\nCHIMERSTRY VISUAL LANGUAGE — Establish a consistent supernatural shorthand distinct from Blood Sorcery. Chimerstry appears as soft, slightly luminous violet-purple smoke around the outer boundary of an illusion, while the interior of that smoky boundary depicts the illusion itself as a coherent, fully rendered scene. The smoke is a frame or threshold, not an opaque cloud hiding the illusion. For discrete illusionary people, duplicates, vehicles, debris, or other objects, render them completely and realistically but make their colors subtly brighter and more saturated than the real environment, with their silhouettes thinly limned by the same violet-purple vapor. Portions beginning to fail may unravel into that purple smoke. Never use red or crimson smoke for Chimerstry, and never depict it as skeins of light, blood magic, generic energy, or fog with nothing visible inside.\n\nCAMERA DIRECTION — Treat camera placement as an expressive tool rather than a default gimmick. Across a four-quad sampler, most concepts may use clear conventional cinematic framing, but one or two quads may use a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder view, foreground obstruction, or another unusual viewpoint where it materially intensifies danger, power, vulnerability, surveillance, speed, or disorientation. Do not force an unconventional angle into every quad. Avoid extreme fisheye distortion, novelty angles, broken anatomy, unreadable action, or compositions that sacrifice the calm overlay area. When a quad specifies an angle, honor it in the final image.\n\nAll four concepts take place outdoors on the streets of Los Angeles at night during the violent climax of the 1944 Second Anarch Revolt. Establish burning façades, flames, smoke, wet pavement, halted streetcars or period automobiles, searchlights, neon haze, barricades, and armed Anarch combatants without graphic gore. Lucien uses Chimerstry as distraction, terror, concealment, and battlefield misdirection; illusions cannot physically touch anyone, so subjects must react before apparent impact. Chimerstry must not resemble blood sorcery: no blood threads, ritual circles, sigils, lightning, or energy beams from Lucien's hands. Lucien remains a slightly cocky, charismatic socialite even under pressure—alert, expressive, and self-possessed, with an exhilarated half-smile where appropriate rather than a blank stare. Every quad must show active interaction rather than characters posing. Keep a calm dark area within each composition for eventual time, location, and narrative overlays. Do not depict Damien Abanda in any quad.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nUse the approved low street-level three-quarter camera and preserve the approved composition: real Anarchs occupy the left side, the single illusionary sedan occupies the middle distance, Lucien remains on the far right, and abandoned weapons dominate the immediate foreground. Make the sedan's direction spatially unmistakable: horizontally mirror the sedan itself relative to the prior final image while leaving its position and every other element unchanged. Its FRONT GRILLE AND HEADLIGHTS must point diagonally LEFT toward the diving Anarchs; its REAR AND TRUNK must point RIGHT toward Lucien. The sedan travels leftward, away from Lucien, cutting off the Anarchs' approach to the foreground weapons. Lucien's head must turn distinctly down and left, and his eyes must be visibly fixed on the abandoned pistols, clubs, shotgun, and other weapons at the bottom foreground—not on the car, not on the Anarchs, and not straight ahead. He is already moving to claim them, wearing a sharp, exhilarated half-smile. The illusionary 1940s sedan is the only localized Chimerstry illusion. It is fully rendered and coherent, with its silhouette, tire spray, and trailing edge framed by predominantly deep-crimson smoke containing only restrained violet-purple sparks and narrow purple streamers; its rear begins to unravel into that red smoke with purple highlights. Do not add illusionary people, duplicates, secondary vehicles, altered façades, disguised objects, or multiple separated effects. Preserve the remaining characters, weapons, firelit 1944 Los Angeles street, palette, lighting, camera angle, anatomy, and negative space.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nOn a burning boulevard outside an Art Deco cinema, Lucien runs diagonally through the frame while three convincing illusionary duplicates of him split in different directions. Each duplicate is fully rendered, subtly brighter and more saturated than the real scene, and thinly limned by violet-purple smoke. Armed Anarchs swing their weapons toward the wrong targets and shout contradictory warnings; one false Lucien vaults a barricade while another begins dissolving into purple vapor at the edge of an alley. The real Lucien, identifiable from the reference and wearing a cocky grin, uses their confusion to pull a wounded generic Camarilla courtier toward cover. Flaming posters, a halted streetcar, broken neon, and searchlights make the revolt unmistakable.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nUse a restrained Dutch angle from beneath the blazing theatre marquee so the tilting architecture intensifies the apparent collapse while faces, movement, and the escape route remain immediately readable. Beneath the marquee, Lucien creates the illusion that the building's stone façade and heavy sign are collapsing into the street. The complete, coherent false collapse occupies the interior of a broad boundary of slightly luminous violet-purple smoke; individual illusionary masonry fragments are subtly brighter than the real environment and thinly rimmed in the same vapor. Anarch riflemen recoil, leap from their firing positions, and shield themselves before the apparent debris can touch them. The foremost fragments dissolve into purple smoke inches above the pavement. Lucien darts through the suddenly cleared route with coat flying, one hand beckoning generic Camarilla survivors after him. Fire engines, overturned period cars, drifting ash, and armed figures deeper in the street sustain the violent 1944 uprising.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a barricaded nighttime avenue, Lucien strides beside a burning automobile while a vast illusion of disciplined Camarilla reinforcements appears across the rooftops and at the far end of the street. The phantom soldiers are fully rendered and slightly brighter and more saturated than reality, every silhouette thinly limned by violet-purple smoke; the space inside the smoky contours contains the coherent false army rather than empty fog. They aim weapons and advance with impossible confidence, forcing a larger Anarch group to turn, scatter, and redeploy while the real handful of Camarilla survivors escapes through a side street. Lucien directs the retreat with a charismatic theatrical gesture and defiant half-smirk as the false army's outer ranks begin unraveling into purple vapor against searchlit clouds.",
