    blindfoldURL = "At a snow-dark Brașov posting inn in 1833, Aishe supervises trunks being strapped to a westbound carriage while her now-grown children take leave of her. Andrei Strandza gestures impatiently toward the road and a travel itinerary, eager for foreign vice; Aishe holds the household keys and looks back toward the city, weighing duty against the first possibility of another life. Frame from behind the carriage wheel for a dynamic, departure-ready foreground.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Aishe-2, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/aishe.webp` as the exact identity reference for Aishe Tache; preserve her facial structure, build, apparent adult age, and commanding beauty while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Andrei Strandza.webp` as exact identity reference for Andrei Strandza; preserve that character’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing, grooming, and accessories to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all four concepts within 1799–1833, Brașov, Romania. Aishe is mortal across this span: allow the quads to show her at different life stages while retaining a recognizable family resemblance to the adult reference; she must age naturally rather than remain vampirically unchanged. Adapt every costume, hairstyle, furnishing, vehicle, weapon, street, and social custom to the specific decade shown in its quad. Aishe is poised, incisive, socially commanding, and difficult to read; show her actively making choices, reading people, negotiating, protecting, manipulating, or surviving rather than passively posing. Her Tarot and visions may be suggested through cards, reflections, prophetic shadows, or restrained double exposure, never generic magical beams or colorful fantasy spell effects.\n\nAISHE’S PHYSIQUE — Treat Aishe’s body shape as an identity invariant in every quad. She is tall, broad-framed, big-boned, and visibly full-figured, with substantial shoulders, arms, hips, thighs, and a soft but powerful build. Do not slim, narrow, or delicately proportion her, and do not depict a pregnancy silhouette. Keep her hands actively occupied, gesturing, braced on furniture, holding an object, or relaxed at her sides—never resting on, cradling, or protectively framing her stomach.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Across the sampler, use mostly clear cinematic framing, but give one or two quads a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder viewpoint, or foreground obstruction where it strengthens power, vulnerability, surveillance, or disorientation. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, pin-up posing, romanticized intimacy, or static character lineups. Keep named figures visually separated enough to read as active participants. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later time, location, and narrative overlays. No montage within a quad, no captions, labels, logos, borders beyond the central gutter, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nFrom a slightly elevated doorway view in a prosperous but socially marginal Brașov merchant house, adolescent Aishe pauses on the stair and listens while her father negotiates her future with minor nobles below. Ledgers, sealed contracts without readable writing, household keys, dowry chests, and winter light make clear that wealth and Aishe herself are being treated as assets. She watches with controlled intelligence rather than helplessness, already calculating how to survive the bargain.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a formal Strandza parlor on the night of her arranged marriage, young adult Aishe stands beside Andrei Strandza before assembled relatives and clergy. Andrei is older, self-satisfied, and distracted by wine; Aishe quietly intercepts the household keys from a servant and studies the indebted estate ledger, claiming practical control even as the ceremony claims her. Use a restrained low angle that makes her composure dominate the room without turning the scene romantic.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nYears later in the busy Strandza household, mature Aishe commands a simultaneous crisis: one hand directs servants carrying medicine toward a sick child while the other closes an account book against an impatient creditor. Her three children appear as unnamed figures of different ages amid tutors, kitchen staff, visiting relations, and Andrei’s discarded coat. The frozen moment should convey motherhood, financial discipline, reputation management, and a woman exercising real authority inside constrained circumstances.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a snow-dark Brașov posting inn in 1833, Aishe supervises trunks being strapped to a westbound carriage while her now-grown children take leave of her. Andrei Strandza gestures impatiently toward the road and a travel itinerary, eager for foreign vice; Aishe holds the household keys and looks back toward the city, weighing duty against the first possibility of another life. Frame from behind the carriage wheel for a dynamic, departure-ready foreground.",
