    blindfoldURL = "During Union occupation in 1865, Aishe enters their shared Creole home through a checkpoint-darkened street and discovers Lady Aveline Dubois gone. Wind from an open balcony scatters cards and curtains around a single terse note with no readable text; military lamps, distant gunboats, shortages, and freed families moving through the street place the private abandonment inside a transformed city. Aishe grips the table rather than collapsing, already forcing herself to plan the first night alone.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Aishe-7, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/aishe.webp` as the exact identity reference for Aishe Tache; preserve her facial structure, build, apparent adult age, and commanding beauty while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Lady Aveline Dubois.webp`, `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Andrei Strandza.webp` as exact identity references for Lady Aveline Dubois and Andrei Strandza; preserve each character’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing, grooming, and accessories to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all four concepts within 1833–1865, New Orleans, United States. Aishe is an ageless vampire after her Embrace: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads even when the depicted decade changes. Adapt every costume, hairstyle, furnishing, vehicle, weapon, street, and social custom to the specific decade shown in its quad. Aishe is poised, incisive, socially commanding, and difficult to read; show her actively making choices, reading people, negotiating, protecting, manipulating, or surviving rather than passively posing. Her Tarot and visions may be suggested through cards, reflections, prophetic shadows, or restrained double exposure, never generic magical beams or colorful fantasy spell effects.\n\nAISHE’S PHYSIQUE — Treat Aishe’s body shape as an identity invariant in every quad. She is tall, broad-framed, big-boned, and visibly full-figured, with substantial shoulders, arms, hips, thighs, and a soft but powerful build. Do not slim, narrow, or delicately proportion her, and do not depict a pregnancy silhouette. Keep her hands actively occupied, gesturing, braced on furniture, holding an object, or relaxed at her sides—never resting on, cradling, or protectively framing her stomach.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Across the sampler, use mostly clear cinematic framing, but give one or two quads a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder viewpoint, or foreground obstruction where it strengthens power, vulnerability, surveillance, or disorientation. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, pin-up posing, romanticized intimacy, or static character lineups. Keep named figures visually separated enough to read as active participants. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later time, location, and narrative overlays. No montage within a quad, no captions, labels, logos, borders beyond the central gutter, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn an opulent but intimate Creole occult parlor in antebellum New Orleans, Lady Aveline Dubois turns a Tarot card toward newly arrived mortal Aishe while Andrei Strandza drinks and flirts noisily with unnamed guests across the room. Aishe leans over the table, captivated by Aveline’s insight rather than posed for romance; candlelight, humid shutters, occult curios, and distant port traffic show the opening through which companionship and danger enter her life.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nImmediately after Aishe’s Embrace in the couple’s rented lodgings, use a restrained Dutch angle from floor level: Andrei Strandza is almost entirely hidden from view behind a toppled folding screen and overturned furniture, his abandoned personal effects providing the only clear sign of irreversible loss. Aishe recoils in horror from what her Hunger has done, dishevelled and stunned but with no visible wounds or blood. Lady Aveline Dubois stands several paces away, urgently directing servants to restore order and remove evidence. Aishe’s shock, the practical cover-up, and the sudden inversion of her marriage should dominate without depicting a body, injury, gore, or sensuality.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn Lady Aveline Dubois’s household years later, Aishe and her sire conduct a tense midnight divination for frightened petitioners. Aveline moves rapidly among pinned maps, covered mirrors, and scattered cards in a manic burst of insight while Aishe calmly catches the useful truth, restrains an alarmed servant, and turns the reading into a concrete decision. The scene should show tutelage, love expressed through difficult collaboration, the Cobweb’s pressure, and Aishe becoming the steadier oracle.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nDuring Union occupation in 1865, Aishe enters their shared Creole home through a checkpoint-darkened street and discovers Lady Aveline Dubois gone. Wind from an open balcony scatters cards and curtains around a single terse note with no readable text; military lamps, distant gunboats, shortages, and freed families moving through the street place the private abandonment inside a transformed city. Aishe grips the table rather than collapsing, already forcing herself to plan the first night alone.",
