    blindfoldURL = "In 1997, Lady Aveline Dubois appears in the doorway of Aishe’s shop after more than a century. The two women are caught in a tense, non-romantic argument across the reading table: Aveline points accusingly toward Camarilla correspondence, while Aishe holds up the mistaken CN Tower postcard and a decisive Tarot card. Years of letters and memory crowd the room. Their physical separation, guarded expressions, and emphatic gestures should convey an estranged sire-and-childe bond, betrayal, prophecy, and the choice that sends Aishe north.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Aishe-28, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/aishe.webp` as the exact identity reference for Aishe Tache; preserve her facial structure, build, apparent adult age, and commanding beauty while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Prince Marcel Guilbeau.webp`, `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Lady Aveline Dubois.webp` as exact identity references for Marcel Guilbeau and Lady Aveline Dubois; preserve each character’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing, grooming, and accessories to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all four concepts within 1983–1997, New Orleans, United States. Aishe is an ageless vampire after her Embrace: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads even when the depicted decade changes. Adapt every costume, hairstyle, furnishing, vehicle, weapon, street, and social custom to the specific decade shown in its quad. Aishe is poised, incisive, socially commanding, and difficult to read; show her actively making choices, reading people, negotiating, protecting, manipulating, or surviving rather than passively posing. Her Tarot and visions may be suggested through cards, reflections, prophetic shadows, or restrained double exposure, never generic magical beams or colorful fantasy spell effects.\n\nAISHE’S PHYSIQUE — Treat Aishe’s body shape as an identity invariant in every quad. She is tall, broad-framed, big-boned, and visibly full-figured, with substantial shoulders, arms, hips, thighs, and a soft but powerful build. Do not slim, narrow, or delicately proportion her, and do not depict a pregnancy silhouette. Keep her hands actively occupied, gesturing, braced on furniture, holding an object, or relaxed at her sides—never resting on, cradling, or protectively framing her stomach.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Across the sampler, use mostly clear cinematic framing, but give one or two quads a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder viewpoint, or foreground obstruction where it strengthens power, vulnerability, surveillance, or disorientation. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, pin-up posing, romanticized intimacy, or static character lineups. Keep named figures visually separated enough to read as active participants. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later time, location, and narrative overlays. No montage within a quad, no captions, labels, logos, borders beyond the central gutter, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nDuring the 1984 World’s Fair era, Aishe stands before Marcel Guilbeau in a restored Creole court while developers, tourism officials, musicians, and Kindred petitioners press competing plans across a table. Marcel points toward glittering riverfront models; Aishe slides a warning card over a threatened neighborhood on the map. The scene should show her usefulness to a stagnant prince and her growing discomfort with reinvestment built on displacement.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn Aishe’s increasingly cluttered fortune shop during the AIDS crisis, she closes the front door against an aggressive vice officer while grieving clients and an exhausted caregiver gather inside. Candles, answering-machine lights, old letters, cards, and memorial photographs without readable text surround her. Aishe directs one client toward medicine and another toward a safe rear exit, making care, secrecy, and community survival more important than occult spectacle.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nOn a humid 1990s night in the French Quarter, Aishe confronts an occult-tour operator who has copied her persona and is exploiting frightened tourists. She catches his fraudulent props in one hand while turning a genuine card toward a plainclothes officer approaching through the crowd. Neon, live music, modern cameras, security grilles, and riverfront commerce convey a city selling mystique while Aishe decides which truths to expose.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn 1997, Lady Aveline Dubois appears in the doorway of Aishe’s shop after more than a century. The two women are caught in a tense, non-romantic argument across the reading table: Aveline points accusingly toward Camarilla correspondence, while Aishe holds up the mistaken CN Tower postcard and a decisive Tarot card. Years of letters and memory crowd the room. Their physical separation, guarded expressions, and emphatic gestures should convey an estranged sire-and-childe bond, betrayal, prophecy, and the choice that sends Aishe north.",
