    blindfoldURL = "During the 2010 summit protests, Aishe stands inside a glass-and-brick downtown lobby between frightened civilians, riot police visible beyond security grilles, and a Camarilla courier demanding immediate passage. She reads the reflections in a dark window, pushes the courier toward a safer service corridor, and opens another door for trapped protesters. Phones, surveillance cameras, condo construction, winter rain, and red emergency light show an old oracle mastering a rapidly modernizing city.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Aishe-30, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs; do not merely mention them in text. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` and use it only as a rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/aishe.webp` as the exact identity reference for Aishe Tache; preserve her facial structure, build, apparent adult age, and commanding beauty while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Prince Maximillian Steele.webp` as exact identity reference for Maximillian Steele; preserve that character’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing, grooming, and accessories to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all four concepts within 1997–2016, Toronto, Canada. Aishe is an ageless vampire after her Embrace: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads even when the depicted decade changes. Adapt every costume, hairstyle, furnishing, vehicle, weapon, street, and social custom to the specific decade shown in its quad. Aishe is poised, incisive, socially commanding, and difficult to read; show her actively making choices, reading people, negotiating, protecting, manipulating, or surviving rather than passively posing. Her Tarot and visions may be suggested through cards, reflections, prophetic shadows, or restrained double exposure, never generic magical beams or colorful fantasy spell effects.\n\nAISHE’S PHYSIQUE — Treat Aishe’s body shape as an identity invariant in every quad. She is tall, broad-framed, big-boned, and visibly full-figured, with substantial shoulders, arms, hips, thighs, and a soft but powerful build. Do not slim, narrow, or delicately proportion her, and do not depict a pregnancy silhouette. Keep her hands actively occupied, gesturing, braced on furniture, holding an object, or relaxed at her sides—never resting on, cradling, or protectively framing her stomach.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Across the sampler, use mostly clear cinematic framing, but give one or two quads a purposeful low angle, high angle, restrained Dutch tilt, over-the-shoulder viewpoint, or foreground obstruction where it strengthens power, vulnerability, surveillance, or disorientation. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, pin-up posing, romanticized intimacy, or static character lineups. Keep named figures visually separated enough to read as active participants. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later time, location, and narrative overlays. No montage within a quad, no captions, labels, logos, borders beyond the central gutter, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt Union Station on a rain-slick night in 1997, Aishe stands amid luggage, porters, pay phones, and late-century commuters, comparing the CN Tower outside with the postcard that sent her to the wrong Canadian city. She catches a pickpocket’s wrist without looking while pointing a driver toward her trunks, instantly adapting rather than appearing lost. Use a high, slightly oblique station viewpoint that preserves her face and the city’s monumental arrival architecture.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a severe Toronto Elysium, Aishe presents herself before Iron Prince Maximillian Steele and his guarded court. Steele questions her history and allegiance from a raised seat; Aishe calmly places Doran’s token and a Tarot card on the table, then turns to answer a hostile Primogen before the Prince can dismiss her. Formal late-1990s tailoring, winter coats, stone interiors, and restrained red heraldic accents make recognition feel earned rather than ceremonial.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nDuring the 2003 blackout, Aishe runs a candlelit reading and improvised neighborhood refuge from an occult storefront while Toronto’s towers go dark outside. She directs a diabetic elder toward stored supplies, warns a student away from an unsafe street, and uses a battery radio and old cards side by side. The scene should capture SARS-era anxiety, immigrant community ties, prophecy used practically, and Aishe building belonging through competence.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nDuring the 2010 summit protests, Aishe stands inside a glass-and-brick downtown lobby between frightened civilians, riot police visible beyond security grilles, and a Camarilla courier demanding immediate passage. She reads the reflections in a dark window, pushes the courier toward a safer service corridor, and opens another door for trapped protesters. Phones, surveillance cameras, condo construction, winter rain, and red emergency light show an old oracle mastering a rapidly modernizing city.",
