    blindfoldURL = "The camera is positioned high in one corner of the cellar at a restrained downward angle. The complete interaction geometry is visible without becoming diagrammatic: the single goblet is resting at the exact center of the glowing tabletop circle; short Black Caesar is leaning out of the chair toward it; red-white binding bands are travelling from Jervais's outstretched open palm directly to Caesar and wrapping around him; and Jervais's opposite index fingertip is pressed against a harbor location on the large wall map. Caesar's head is angled toward the goblet with hungry red-rimmed eyes and exposed fangs. Jervais's head is angled toward Caesar with a controlled half-smile. The high view is keeping both hands of Jervais unobscured and is making the source and destination of every magical band unmistakable.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-8, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter must separate the quads, with no visual content crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, words, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/black-caesar.webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He must retain the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; beside Jervais, the top of his head and shoulders are visibly lower. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Jervais de la Croix.webp` as the exact identity reference for Jervais de la Croix; preserve his referenced facial structure, complexion, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting his clothing to 1730s Spanish Florida.\n\nSAMPLER PURPOSE — All four quads are depicting alternative framings of the same single frozen instant inside the same sealed coquina cellar shortly after Caesar's Embrace. They are testing which composition most clearly communicates three simultaneous facts: Caesar is fighting the magical restraint to reach one goblet; Jervais's outstretched palm is visibly creating the binding energy; and Jervais's other fingertip is physically touching a specific point on a harbor map. The alternatives may vary camera height and foreground geometry, but those three facts and the character identities must remain unchanged.\n\nCORE STAGING — Newly Embraced Black Caesar is straining forward from a rough wooden chair toward exactly one silver goblet filled with dark-red blood. The goblet is resting upright at the center of a simple glowing geometric circle inscribed on the tabletop; nobody is holding it. Caesar's red-rimmed eyes are fixed on the goblet, his fangs are fully visible, his brows are drawn down, and his mouth is open in a near-frenzied snarl. Several clean red-white bands of Blood Sorcery are emerging directly from the open palm of one of Jervais's outstretched hands, crossing visible space, and ending as tight luminous restraints around Caesar's chest, arms, and chair. Jervais's other hand is reaching back to the wall, and that hand's index fingertip is remaining in direct physical contact with one specific location on a large harbor map pinned flat to the stone. Jervais is looking toward Caesar with raised brows and a controlled, taunting half-smile. One low oil lamp is lighting the cellar; the windows are sealed or black with night.\n\nVISUAL RULES — Each quad is depicting one decisive still image, not a synopsis or action sequence. Every person has one principal pose, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean glowing red-white bands and a restrained geometric circle, not webbing. The binding bands originate only at Jervais's open palm. No energy originates from the goblet, tabletop circle, floor, ceiling, or offscreen. Jervais's map-touching finger is physically contacting the map rather than pointing into open air. Keep the goblet resting on the table rather than in any hand. Render clothing, mapmaking, furniture, masonry, and lighting accurately for 1730s Spanish Florida. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail area for later overlay text. No additional people, captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nThe camera is positioned at goblet height beside the near edge of the table. The single silver goblet is standing in the immediate foreground at the center of the glowing tabletop circle. Beyond it, short Black Caesar is straining forward from the chair with one reaching hand aligned directly toward the goblet, his red-rimmed eyes fixed on it and his fanged snarl fully visible. Jervais is standing in the right middle ground. His nearer open palm is facing Caesar and is visibly emitting the red-white binding bands that travel from his palm to Caesar's body. His farther arm is extended backward to the wall, with the index fingertip pressed flat against one marked harbor entrance on the map. Jervais's face is turned toward Caesar. The goblet, Caesar's reaching hand, Jervais's emitting palm, and the fingertip touching the map form one readable diagonal.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nThe camera is positioned just behind Jervais's map-side shoulder, looking along both of his arms. Jervais's left index fingertip is pressed firmly onto a specific harbor entrance on the wall map in the near foreground. His right arm is extending across the frame toward Caesar, with the open right palm fully visible as the sole source of several red-white binding bands. At the far end of those bands, short Black Caesar is twisting forward in the chair toward the single goblet resting inside the glowing tabletop circle. Caesar's eyes are locked on the goblet, his fangs are exposed, and his face is contorted by desperate hunger. Jervais is glancing sideways toward Caesar with a small taunting smile. The composition must keep the fingertip-to-map contact, open emitting palm, restraints, Caesar, and goblet simultaneously visible.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nThe camera is positioned beside Caesar's reaching forearm at chair height, creating a tense close foreground. Short Black Caesar is occupying the left foreground, pulling hard against red-white bands wrapped around his chest and arms while stretching his hand toward the single silver goblet resting untouched inside the glowing circle on the table. His gaze is fixed only on the goblet; his red-rimmed eyes, bared fangs, furrowed brows, and open snarl are clearly visible. Jervais is occupying the right background in full view. One of his open palms is aimed squarely at Caesar and is emitting every visible binding band. His opposite arm is reaching to the map behind him, and that index fingertip is visibly planted on one specific point rather than hovering. Jervais is watching Caesar with calm amusement.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nThe camera is positioned high in one corner of the cellar at a restrained downward angle. The complete interaction geometry is visible without becoming diagrammatic: the single goblet is resting at the exact center of the glowing tabletop circle; short Black Caesar is leaning out of the chair toward it; red-white binding bands are travelling from Jervais's outstretched open palm directly to Caesar and wrapping around him; and Jervais's opposite index fingertip is pressed against a harbor location on the large wall map. Caesar's head is angled toward the goblet with hungry red-rimmed eyes and exposed fangs. Jervais's head is angled toward Caesar with a controlled half-smile. The high view is keeping both hands of Jervais unobscured and is making the source and destination of every magical band unmistakable.",
