    blindfoldURL = "In a flooded New Orleans courtyard under a storm-black night sky, Black Caesar is standing on the broad stone base of a fountain so that his short body is elevated above the surrounding crowd and floodwater. His face is completely clean-shaven. He is holding a revolver safely by its barrel and is extending the grip first toward an armed agent standing knee-deep below him. Caesar is looking directly at the agent with an urgent, commanding expression—eyes wide, brows lowered, mouth open in a short order. The agent is reaching for the offered grip while meeting Caesar's gaze. Dockworkers, priests, healers, revenants, and families are moving through the water behind them beneath driving rain and dark lantern light. The camera is at water level beside the agent's shoulder, making the grip-first handoff and Caesar's raised position unmistakable.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-22, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad is occupying exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter is separating the quads, with no figures, architecture, smoke, weather, ships, or lighting crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, text, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/black-caesar.webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He is retaining the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; when he is standing beside other adult men, the top of his head and his shoulders are visibly lower than theirs. His authority is being communicated through posture, skill, attention, and others' reactions rather than height or bulk. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/The Baron's Bleak Bokor.webp` as the identity reference for The Baron's Bleak Bokor; preserve the referenced face, apparent age, complexion, build, hair, and distinguishing features while adapting clothing and grooming to the depicted decade. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/composition/black-caesar-lwa-possession-panel-reference.png` only as a composition reference for making a spirit manifestation or overlapping human-and-spirit silhouette spatially legible; its exact pose, people, setting, clothing, and framing are not source content.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is depicting one decisive instant in one location, not a scene summary, montage, or sequence. Every featured person is having one principal pose or physical action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative context is being shown only through bodies, spatial relationships, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence. Each quad is remaining understandable without knowledge of Vampire: the Masquerade terminology.\n\nPERIOD — All four concepts are taking place within 1880–1894, New Orleans, United States. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period. His clean-shaven face and short, compact stature are visible in every quad. Exterior views are taking place at night or in storm-black conditions. Ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport are being rendered accurately for the relevant decade and geography. Colonial violence, slavery, racial oppression, warfare, and religious practice are being treated with gravity rather than adventure-romance or exotic spectacle.\n\nSUPERNATURAL VISUAL LANGUAGE — Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean, glowing red-white lines of energy, geometric seals, or luminous contours rather than webbing. Voodoo ritual geometry is appearing as recognizable veves: flowing symmetrical linework with crossroads, curves, and ritual flourishes rather than alchemical circles or generic pentagrams. Ghosts and wraiths are appearing as cold ash-grey translucent human forms, breath-like mist, or displaced shadows.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — The four alternatives are using meaningfully different framing: eye-level interaction, low foreground angle, high or overhead angle, over-the-shoulder view, restrained Dutch tilt, or foreground obstruction where useful. Every angle is preserving readable anatomy, expressions, eyelines, and the focal interaction. Named figures are remaining visually distinct and sufficiently separated. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nInside a gaslit New Orleans riverfront warehouse at night, Black Caesar is pressing one hand onto the lid of a ritual cargo crate while sliding legitimate customs papers over a small pile of bribe money with his other hand. He is visibly shorter than the customs official opposite him. Caesar is looking up into the official's face with narrowed eyes and a controlled half-smile. The official is staring down at the covered money with tense lips and one hand hovering above the papers. Dockworkers and merchants are standing still at a respectful distance, watching the exchange. Iron balconies, levee machinery, and moored riverboats are visible through open doors against complete darkness. The camera is at crate height on a slight Dutch angle, aligning Caesar's hands, the bribe, and the official's eyeline.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a candlelit New Orleans cemetery chamber, Black Caesar and The Baron's Bleak Bokor are standing outside opposite sides of a large flowing Voodoo veve drawn on the stone floor. Caesar is short and clean-shaven; the Bokor is taller and is wearing no sunglasses. His mysterious brown eyes are fully visible, with his facial makeup continuing around them. Both men are extending one hand toward the veve, and separate clean red-white streamers of energy are flowing from their fingertips into its curved crossroads linework. An ash-grey wraith is rising vertically from the centre. Caesar is staring at the wraith with narrowed concentration; the Bokor is also watching it with lowered brows and a solemn, painted mouth. Mourners, healers, and assistants are forming a distant semicircle. The camera is high and slightly off-centre, clearly showing both casters outside the veve and the two energy paths joining it.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a grand Creole salon during a nighttime Mardi Gras gathering, Black Caesar is closing one hand over the wrist of a masked guest whose fingers are wrapped around a small glass spirit vessel. Caesar is visibly shorter than the guest and the surrounding adult men. He is looking up into the guest's eyes with lowered brows and a thin, dangerous smile. The guest is staring down at Caesar's hand with widened eyes and a stiff, startled mouth. Musicians are continuing to play in the background while masked politicians, criminals, vampires, and ritual specialists are turning their heads toward the confrontation. Deep-red costume accents are punctuating the monochrome room. The camera is close at vessel height, with the intercepted hand in the foreground and Caesar's clean-shaven expression immediately beyond it.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn a flooded New Orleans courtyard under a storm-black night sky, Black Caesar is standing on the broad stone base of a fountain so that his short body is elevated above the surrounding crowd and floodwater. His face is completely clean-shaven. He is holding a revolver safely by its barrel and is extending the grip first toward an armed agent standing knee-deep below him. Caesar is looking directly at the agent with an urgent, commanding expression—eyes wide, brows lowered, mouth open in a short order. The agent is reaching for the offered grip while meeting Caesar's gaze. Dockworkers, priests, healers, revenants, and families are moving through the water behind them beneath driving rain and dark lantern light. The camera is at water level beside the agent's shoulder, making the grip-first handoff and Caesar's raised position unmistakable.",
