    blindfoldURL = "On a winter railway platform in Vienna at night in 1912, Black Caesar is holding a closed leather document folder against his chest while facing a westbound train. His body is angled toward the carriage door, but his face is turned back toward Jervais de la Croix; Caesar's eyes are narrowed and his mouth is pressed into restrained disgust. Jervais is standing one pace behind him, extending one sealed order toward Caesar with a commanding expression and chin raised. Three Ducheski revenant workers are loading occult trunks into a baggage car while watching Caesar for direction. These revenants look completely human: ordinary living-looking adult men and women with natural complexions, normal eyes, normal teeth, healthy human facial proportions, and practical railway-worker clothing. Their nature is suggested only by disciplined obedience and discreet matching family insignia, not by monstrous anatomy. Dense steam, electric station lamps, snow, and iron roof trusses are framing the two men. The camera is low behind one trunk on a baggage cart, with the sealed order, Caesar's backward eyeline, and the train door forming a visual triangle.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-23, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad is occupying exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter is separating the quads, with no visual content crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, words, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/black-caesar.webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He is retaining the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; beside standing adult men, the top of his head and shoulders are visibly lower than theirs. His authority is being communicated through posture, skill, attention, and others' reactions rather than height or bulk. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Jervais de la Croix.webp` as the identity reference for Jervais de la Croix; preserve the referenced facial structure, complexion, distinguishing features, and recognizable identity while adapting apparent age, supernatural state, clothing, and grooming only as explicitly required by a quad.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is depicting one decisive instant in one location, not a synopsis, montage, or sequence. Every featured person is having one principal pose or physical action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative context is being communicated only through bodies, spatial relationships, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence. Each quad is remaining intelligible without knowledge of Vampire: the Masquerade terminology.\n\nPERIOD — All concepts are taking place within 1894–1912, Vienna, Austria. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period. Exterior scenes are taking place at night, and interiors are lit by candles or early electric lamps with dark windows. Ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport are being rendered accurately for the relevant decade and geography. Colonial violence, slavery, racial oppression, warfare, and religious practice are being treated with gravity rather than adventure-romance or exotic spectacle.\n\nSUPERNATURAL VISUAL LANGUAGE — Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean, glowing red-white lines of energy, geometric seals, or luminous contours rather than webbing. Voodoo ritual geometry is appearing as recognizable veves: flowing symmetrical linework with crossroads, curves, and ritual flourishes rather than alchemical circles or generic pentagrams. Wraiths are appearing as cold ash-grey translucent human forms with softened lower bodies, drifting edges, and the recognizable faces and period clothing of the dead.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — The alternatives are exploring meaningfully different framing: eye-level interaction, low foreground angle, high or overhead angle, over-the-shoulder view, restrained Dutch tilt, or foreground obstruction where useful. Every angle is preserving readable anatomy, expressions, eyelines, stature, and focal interaction. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nInside an ornate Viennese occult council chamber lit dimly by early electric lamps, Black Caesar is standing alone at the left side of a long table across from Jervais de la Croix on the right. Caesar is shorter than every surrounding official. An old shipping map is lying flat across the table, with loose pages bearing black geometric veves around its edges. Caesar is pointing at one location on the map while his face is turned upward toward Jervais; his eyebrows are raised and his mouth is tense and slightly open. A suited courtier immediately behind Caesar is gripping Caesar's shoulder and pulling backward. Jervais's head and eyes are turned fully away from Caesar and directly toward that courtier. Jervais's pupils are fixed on the courtier's face, his brows are lowered in stern reproach, and one raised index finger is held between them in a clear staying gesture. Two men and one woman in severe aristocratic clothing are watching from the background with raised chins, narrowed eyes, and faint sneers. The camera is positioned low at the near edge of the table, angled upward over the map so the gripping hand, Jervais's unmistakable eyeline toward the courtier, and his raised finger are all unobscured.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside a large Viennese archive filled with tall shelves of old books and unlabelled document boxes, a dark wooden desk is bare except for a thin manila envelope and a large arcane circle inscribed directly into the tabletop. The circle is glowing with intense deep-red light and is casting ominous red illumination upward across the envelope, Black Caesar, and an investigator. Caesar is holding the envelope above the circle with the wax seal angled toward his face. One large red wax seal bearing a geometric glyph is glowing with exactly the same red light and is belching a dense plume of inky black smoke upward. There is no connecting lightning and no mechanical apparatus. Caesar's chin is lowered toward the envelope; his face is turned directly toward the smoking wax seal, and both pupils are visibly aimed at the seal itself rather than at the investigator or camera. His eyes are opened wide, his eyebrows are raised high, his head is recoiling slightly, and his lips are parted in visible surprise. The investigator is seen from behind on the opposite side of the desk, leaning backward with tense shoulders and one outstretched hand recoiling from the envelope. The camera is placed just behind the investigator's shoulder so the glowing tabletop circle, smoking seal, and Caesar's seal-directed eyeline form one clear line.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a fin-de-siècle Viennese salon beneath early electric chandeliers, Black Caesar and one foreign envoy are standing partly concealed beside a tall folding-panel privacy screen covered in dark brocade. The screen is an opaque fabric room divider rather than a mirror. Caesar is shorter than the envoy and is leaning close enough to speak privately while keeping their bodies separate. Caesar's left hand is resting firmly on the envoy's near shoulder. Caesar's mouth is visibly open in mid-whisper beside the envoy's ear, his eyes are fixed on the envoy's face, and one eyebrow is raised in warning. The envoy is holding a silver serving platter between them with both hands, one hand visibly supporting each side of the platter. Exactly two goblets are standing on the platter: one contains a clear pale drink, and the other is filled with thick, dark, syrupy red liquid whose glossy surface and deep crimson translucence are unmistakable. The envoy is staring down toward the dark-red goblet with widened eyes, lifted brows, and parted lips. Diplomats, artists, soldiers, and aristocratic guests are conversing indistinctly beyond the privacy screen. The camera is positioned at platter height beside the screen, making Caesar's whispering mouth, hand on the shoulder, the envoy's two hands supporting the platter, the shocked expression, and both goblets simultaneously readable.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nOn a winter railway platform in Vienna at night in 1912, Black Caesar is holding a closed leather document folder against his chest while facing a westbound train. His body is angled toward the carriage door, but his face is turned back toward Jervais de la Croix; Caesar's eyes are narrowed and his mouth is pressed into restrained disgust. Jervais is standing one pace behind him, extending one sealed order toward Caesar with a commanding expression and chin raised. Three Ducheski revenant workers are loading occult trunks into a baggage car while watching Caesar for direction. These revenants look completely human: ordinary living-looking adult men and women with natural complexions, normal eyes, normal teeth, healthy human facial proportions, and practical railway-worker clothing. Their nature is suggested only by disciplined obedience and discreet matching family insignia, not by monstrous anatomy. Dense steam, electric station lamps, snow, and iron roof trusses are framing the two men. The camera is low behind one trunk on a baggage cart, with the sealed order, Caesar's backward eyeline, and the train door forming a visual triangle.",
