    blindfoldURL = "On a barricaded Toledo street under a completely black night sky in the opening violence of 1936, short, clean-shaven Black Caesar is lifting a wounded civilian from wet cobblestones with both arms. His eyes are fixed on the civilian's face, his brows are tightened, and his mouth is open as he is calling for help. A Sabbat courier several paces behind him is carrying an iron-bound occult crate toward a railway entrance while looking back at Caesar. Refugees are moving through a convent gate as rifle flashes illuminate church towers, military cadets, labor banners without readable text, and drifting railway smoke. The camera is at ground level beside the abandoned civilian's satchel, making Caesar's compact body and the rescue the focal action while the war-torn route remains legible behind him.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-28, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Every quad is occupying exactly one quarter of the canvas. A narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter is separating the quads, with no visual content crossing the gutter.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach every named file as an actual generation input. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as a style reference for cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained deep-red accents. Its people, locations, words, symbols, and exact compositions are not source content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/black-caesar.webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar. He is retaining the same facial structure, dark skin, dense curly black hair, compact muscular build, and apparent adult age in every quad. His upper lip, chin, and jaw are completely clean-shaven. He is a short adult man; beside standing adult men, the top of his head and shoulders are visibly lower than theirs. His authority is being communicated through posture, skill, attention, and others' reactions rather than height or bulk. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Jervais de la Croix.webp` as the identity reference for Jervais de la Croix; preserve the referenced facial structure, complexion, distinguishing features, and recognizable identity while adapting apparent age, supernatural state, clothing, and grooming only as explicitly required by a quad. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Pre-Death Jean Ducheski I.webp` as the identity reference for Jean Ducheski I; preserve the referenced facial structure, complexion, distinguishing features, and recognizable identity while adapting apparent age, supernatural state, clothing, and grooming only as explicitly required by a quad. The reference is showing Jean alive. Quad C is depicting him after his 1830 death as a cold ash-grey translucent wraith with the same recognizable face and period sailor's clothing.\n\nFROZEN-IMAGE RULE — Each quad is depicting one decisive instant in one location, not a synopsis, montage, or sequence. Every featured person is having one principal pose or physical action, one explicit eyeline, and one visibly described expression. Narrative context is being communicated only through bodies, spatial relationships, props, architecture, lighting, and background evidence. Each quad is remaining intelligible without knowledge of Vampire: the Masquerade terminology.\n\nPERIOD — All concepts are taking place within 1930–1936, Toledo, Spain. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period. Exterior scenes are taking place at night or during the final dark hour before dawn. No vampire is standing in direct sunlight. Ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport are being rendered accurately for the relevant decade and geography. Colonial violence, slavery, racial oppression, warfare, and religious practice are being treated with gravity rather than adventure-romance or exotic spectacle.\n\nSUPERNATURAL VISUAL LANGUAGE — Blood Sorcery is appearing as a small number of clean, glowing red-white lines of energy, geometric seals, or luminous contours rather than webbing. Voodoo ritual geometry is appearing as recognizable veves: flowing symmetrical linework with crossroads, curves, and ritual flourishes rather than alchemical circles or generic pentagrams. Wraiths are appearing as cold ash-grey translucent human forms with softened lower bodies, drifting edges, and the recognizable faces and period clothing of the dead.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — The alternatives are exploring meaningfully different framing: eye-level interaction, low foreground angle, high or overhead angle, over-the-shoulder view, restrained Dutch tilt, or foreground obstruction where useful. Every angle is preserving readable anatomy, expressions, eyelines, stature, and focal interaction. Each quad is reserving one calm, dark, low-detail region for later overlay text. The complete sampler contains no captions, labels, readable paragraphs, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern objects, graphic gore, fisheye distortion, static lineup, or glossy superhero posing.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nInside Toledo's cathedral archive at night, Black Caesar is standing beside a table of chained manuscripts and is holding an opened hidden ledger toward Jervais de la Croix. Caesar is visibly shorter than Jervais; his clean-shaven face is turned upward, his eyes are fixed on his sire, and his mouth is tightened in accusation. Jervais is standing across the table with one palm raised toward Caesar, projecting a compact red-white geometric ward between them while staring down at Caesar with narrowed eyes. Clergy and servants are watching from a distant stone archway. Tall windows are showing a completely black sky above the old city. The camera is low beside the open ledger, aligning its marked page, Caesar's face, the ward, and Jervais's eyeline.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nOn a fortified Toledo rooftop during the final dark hour before dawn, the camera is positioned just beyond the parapet and is facing inward across the roof. Jervais de la Croix is standing in the immediate foreground facing the camera, with his back completely turned toward the roof behind him. His recognizable face is fully visible; his eyes are looking slightly downward past the camera toward the sleeping city, his expression is distant and unaware, and neither his head nor his gaze is turned toward Black Caesar. Several paces behind Jervais in the same frame, short, clean-shaven Black Caesar is approaching silently while carrying a sharpened wooden stake low in one hand. Caesar's eyes are fixed between Jervais's shoulder blades, his brows are lowered, and his mouth is set in grim resolve. The parapet and Jervais's front-facing figure dominate the foreground while Caesar's compact advancing silhouette and stake remain clearly visible behind him. The black sky is only beginning to lighten into a narrow cold-grey band; sunrise is still roughly an hour away and no direct sunlight is present.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a cellar beneath a working-class Toledo café at night, short, clean-shaven Black Caesar is seated at one side of a rough table opposite two severe Sabbat emissaries. Caesar is pushing a stack of Camarilla documents away from himself with one open palm while staring at the nearest emissary with narrowed eyes and a guarded, unsmiling expression. The emissary is extending an empty open hand toward Caesar, watching him expectantly. Directly behind Caesar's shoulder stands the ash-grey translucent wraith of Jean Ducheski I. Jean must unmistakably match the attached `Pre-Death Jean Ducheski I.webp` identity reference: the same recognizable Black facial structure, deep-brown complexion translated into ash-grey translucency, dark eyes, lean build, long face, and period sailor's clothing. Jean is resting one spectral hand on Caesar's chair back and is looking down at the emissaries with a protective frown. Police boots are visible through a basement window at street level, and red political posters without readable text are hanging on the walls. The camera is over the emissary's shoulder, centering Caesar and Jean while keeping Jean's referenced face clearly visible rather than obscured.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nOn a barricaded Toledo street under a completely black night sky in the opening violence of 1936, short, clean-shaven Black Caesar is lifting a wounded civilian from wet cobblestones with both arms. His eyes are fixed on the civilian's face, his brows are tightened, and his mouth is open as he is calling for help. A Sabbat courier several paces behind him is carrying an iron-bound occult crate toward a railway entrance while looking back at Caesar. Refugees are moving through a convent gate as rifle flashes illuminate church towers, military cadets, labor banners without readable text, and drifting railway smoke. The camera is at ground level beside the abandoned civilian's satchel, making Caesar's compact body and the rescue the focal action while the war-torn route remains legible behind him.",
