    blindfoldURL = "In a snow-slick parking structure near departure, Mortius hands Caesar new papers and keys while hostile witnesses approach from opposite ramps. Caesar directs a driver toward Toronto, blocks one pursuer with the car door, and returns a final sealed favor to Mortius. Milwaukee’s industrial waterfront glows beyond concrete pillars, marking the choice to leave refuge and gamble on a Camarilla future.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for BlackCaesar-37, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, ships, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/black-caesar.webp` as the exact identity reference for Black Caesar; preserve his facial structure, dark skin, powerful build, apparent adult age, and commanding presence while replacing modern clothing and background with historically appropriate content. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Mortius.webp` as exact identity reference for Mortius; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the depicted year.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1998–2002, Milwaukee, United States. Caesar is an ageless vampire throughout this period; preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. Adapt ships, weapons, architecture, uniforms, clothing, furnishings, documents, and transport to the specific decade and geography of each quad. Caesar is a disciplined survivor, mariner, occult operative, and later commander: depict him actively navigating, bargaining, fighting, directing, studying, or choosing—not passively posing. Treat slavery, colonial violence, famine, war, and racial oppression with gravity rather than adventure-romance. Blood Sorcery may appear as restrained geometric skeins or seals of deep-red light. Ghosts, wraiths, and Lwa should appear as cold ash-grey translucence, shadow, breath-like mist, or possession expressed through a host’s body; do not use Chimerstry’s purple smoke language or generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen danger, command, confinement, or surveillance. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, triumphalist colonial imagery, pirate caricature, or glossy superhero posing. Keep named characters sufficiently separated for readable interaction. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn a guarded late-1990s Milwaukee chantry room, purge-scarred Caesar invokes the old Life Boon before Mortius. Caesar places the weathered boon token and his damaged signet on the table; Mortius closes the security shutters and orders suspicious Tremere guards to stand down. Desktop computers, fax machines, paper archives, and winter industrial light make refuge feel conditional and bureaucratic.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nUnder harsh interview lamps, Caesar faces a Camarilla investigator while Mortius observes through glass. Blood samples, sealed evidence, photographs, and contradictory records cover the table. Caesar catches the investigator’s accusation mid-sentence and calmly produces one authentic wartime document among the forgeries, beginning the double-agent story through disciplined performance rather than overt magic.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a paper archive after midnight, Caesar and Mortius rebuild decades of history. Mortius feeds documents into a shredder while Caesar rearranges photographs, correspondence, and House seals across multiple eras; an assistant updates records on a beige computer. Use an overhead view that makes the constructed narrative visually clear without rendering any readable text.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn a snow-slick parking structure near departure, Mortius hands Caesar new papers and keys while hostile witnesses approach from opposite ramps. Caesar directs a driver toward Toronto, blocks one pursuer with the car door, and returns a final sealed favor to Mortius. Milwaukee’s industrial waterfront glows beyond concrete pillars, marking the choice to leave refuge and gamble on a Camarilla future.",
