    blindfoldURL = "At a failing East Coast colonial outpost near the end of the period, mortal Fomórach unloads supplies while Puritan overseers argue over missing food. Drake watches from deep shadow beyond the palisade as Fomórach quietly repeats the overheard plan to an unseen contact and diverts punishment from another servant. Lanterns, raw cabins, forest pressure, and the first hint of predatory red eyes foreshadow the Embrace without completing it.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-1, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Pre-Embrace Fomorach.webp` as the exact identity reference for mortal Fomórach, subject to the mortal/Embrace instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Drake.webp` as exact identity reference for Drake; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1769–1786, Belfast through the East Coast Colonies. The period crosses ghouldom and Embrace: keep Fomórach recognizably the same young man while making the transition from mortal hardship to the visibly inhuman curse of his Nosferatu blood unmistakable. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn daylight outside Fomórach’s crowded ancestral Belfast home, adolescent mortal Fomórach stops his father from selling the family’s final cow while siblings, linen, carpentry tools, dowry goods, and a parish road reveal impossible household choices. He quietly hands over his own small inheritance instead and takes an indenture contract from a waiting recruiter. The moment should show sacrifice, calculation, Catholic family identity, and constrained poverty without sentimentality.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a busy Belfast marketplace, young Fomórach catches a ship agent cheating emigrants on weights and passage terms. He plants one hand on the false scale, points other laborers toward the honest tally, and listens as merchants and sectarian officials argue behind him. Canvas stalls, linen goods, carts, taverns, church spires, and harbor movement frame the choice to leave as both economic necessity and an intelligence test.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nOn an emigrant ship in heavy Atlantic weather, Fomórach crawls along the lower edge of the deck to overhear officers discussing rations and indenture assignments while passengers shelter near guarded hatches. He signals companions toward hidden water casks just before a wave breaks over the rail. Use a low deck-level camera through rigging to show the exposed hierarchy of voyage, covert listening, and survival.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a failing East Coast colonial outpost near the end of the period, mortal Fomórach unloads supplies while Puritan overseers argue over missing food. Drake watches from deep shadow beyond the palisade as Fomórach quietly repeats the overheard plan to an unseen contact and diverts punishment from another servant. Lanterns, raw cabins, forest pressure, and the first hint of predatory red eyes foreshadow the Embrace without completing it.",
