    blindfoldURL = "By the late 1830s, Fomórach emerges from a brick sewer opening into a confident market city and presents Drake with a completed web of keys, maps, and coded objects. Drake releases him from close apprenticeship by returning one old restraint or token. Street lamps, market buildings, taverns, rail planning, and layered cellars show York becoming Toronto as Fomórach claims mastery beneath it.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-8, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/fomorach.webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach, subject to the mortal/Embrace instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Drake.webp` as Drake’s exact appearance reference: his identity remains deliberately unknowable, with his face, head, and skin completely obscured by the same dark wraps in every depiction; never render him bare-faced or conventionally human-looking. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Prince Maximillian Steele.webp` as Maximillian Steele’s exact identity reference; preserve Steele’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting his costume and grooming to the period. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/composition/fomorach-listening-wall-panel-reference.png` only as a composition reference; do not copy its exact setting, figures, or props.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1793–1846, York and early Toronto, Canada. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout this period: preserve the reference identity, severe deformity, powerful frame, and apparently starved, predatory physicality across all four quads. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt the 1793 lakeshore founding of York, Fomórach and Drake stand below a rough survey platform while soldiers and laborers mark roads above. Fomórach presses his ear to newly dug earth and points Drake toward a natural drainage cut that will become their first concealed route. Fort timbers, Indigenous trade canoes, garrison boats, tavern frames, and muddy shoreline show infrastructure and intelligence beginning together.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nDuring the Battle of York, use a canted view from inside a cellar as bombardment collapses the street above. Fomórach braces a beam, drags civilians toward an escape tunnel, and simultaneously watches soldiers carry a strategic chest past the opening. Drake signals from deeper shadow, forcing a choice between rescue and information. Smoke, lake guns, fire, and raw defenses place the scene firmly in 1813.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn 1818, Fomórach accompanies Drake to an austere court audience before Iron Prince Maximillian Steele. Steele points to a city plan and demands hidden access beneath the growing settlement; Drake bargains calmly while Fomórach notices an eavesdropper behind the paneling and silently blocks their escape. The scene should make the Iron Praxis feel like a political settlement built atop Nosferatu knowledge.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nBy the late 1830s, Fomórach emerges from a brick sewer opening into a confident market city and presents Drake with a completed web of keys, maps, and coded objects. Drake releases him from close apprenticeship by returning one old restraint or token. Street lamps, market buildings, taverns, rail planning, and layered cellars show York becoming Toronto as Fomórach claims mastery beneath it.",
