    blindfoldURL = "At a fog-dark railway or dock warehouse, Drake supervises Fomórach’s forced return to Toronto: the staked vampire lies rigid inside an open coffin while servants prepare it for transport. Drake turns from angry London envoys to place his own seal on the crate, accepting the debts his childe created. Frame from inside the coffin lid so Drake, guards, rain, and departure machinery loom overhead without graphic injury.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-15, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/fomorach.webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach, subject to the mortal/Embrace instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Drake.webp` as Drake’s exact appearance reference: his identity remains deliberately unknowable, with his face, head, and skin completely obscured by the same dark wraps in every depiction; never render him bare-faced or conventionally human-looking. Adapt only his outer clothing to the period while preserving the dark wrappings.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1846–1849, Belfast and London, United Kingdom. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout this period: preserve the reference identity, severe deformity, powerful frame, and apparently starved, predatory physicality across all four quads. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn rain at night, Fomórach enters the roofless ruins of his ancestral Belfast home during the Great Famine. He lifts a damaged Catholic devotional object from mud and scattered family possessions while eviction marks, an abandoned hearth, and stripped fields reveal absence rather than a single battle. His monstrous face turns from grief toward rage as distant agents search the road.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a gaslit London rookery, Fomórach hurls an exploitative landlord or agent through a lodging-house doorway while terrified tenants scatter and police lanterns close from both ends of the alley. Use a low, restrained Dutch angle through broken furniture to capture the beginning of his bloody campaign. Keep victims and violence largely obscured; grief curdling into indiscriminate vengeance is the subject.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a hidden London Nosferatu court, Fomórach stands chained before an unnamed Primogen and assembled sewer-dwellers while evidence of burned favors and violated feeding rights covers the table. He snaps one restraint and points toward the aristocratic district above, still demanding justice. Mirrors, maps, listening tubes, and barred tunnels show a sophisticated clan deciding whether mercy is politically affordable.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a fog-dark railway or dock warehouse, Drake supervises Fomórach’s forced return to Toronto: the staked vampire lies rigid inside an open coffin while servants prepare it for transport. Drake turns from angry London envoys to place his own seal on the crate, accepting the debts his childe created. Frame from inside the coffin lid so Drake, guards, rain, and departure machinery loom overhead without graphic injury.",
