    blindfoldURL = "In a sealed rail warehouse, Fomórach Embraces Oksana Mara Ziva as soldiers close outside. She grips him back with ferocious intent while the first signs of the Wendigo curse sharpen her features and hunger. Grain lies locked behind barred doors, making the supernatural act an echo of the surrounding famine. Keep blood minimal and the moral weight of repeating Fomórach’s own lineage unmistakable.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-23, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/fomorach.webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach, subject to the mortal/Embrace instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Pre-Embrace Oksana Ziva.webp` as Oksana’s exact mortal identity reference and `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Oksana 'Mara' Ziva.webp` as Mara’s exact post-Embrace identity reference; use the appropriate version in each quad, preserving her face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1932–1936, Kharkiv and the surrounding Ukrainian countryside. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout this period: preserve the reference identity, severe deformity, powerful frame, and apparently starved, predatory physicality across all four quads. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt a guarded grain rail siding during the Holodomor, Fomórach hides beneath a freight platform and listens as officials divert food away from starving villages. He reaches through shadow to steal a manifest token while soldiers pass within arm’s reach. Empty carts, sealed grain, smoke, snow, and distant civilians establish state-created deprivation; do not turn hunger into picturesque ruin.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn an overwhelmed Kharkiv clinic, Fomórach watches Oksana Mara Ziva refuse her own ration so another patient can eat. She remains active and defiant despite starvation, arguing with an official while helping a child or elder stand. Fomórach studies her from a service corridor, recognizing endurance and rage rather than selecting a passive victim.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nOn an abandoned farm at night, Oksana Mara Ziva catches Fomórach testing her with a concealed food cache and turns a weapon on him instead of taking the bait. He steps from Obfuscate-shadow with empty hands, impressed, while informants and predators search the road beyond. Use a low threshold viewpoint to emphasize mutual suspicion, hunger, and the dangerous logic of his selection.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn a sealed rail warehouse, Fomórach Embraces Oksana Mara Ziva as soldiers close outside. She grips him back with ferocious intent while the first signs of the Wendigo curse sharpen her features and hunger. Grain lies locked behind barred doors, making the supernatural act an echo of the surrounding famine. Keep blood minimal and the moral weight of repeating Fomórach’s own lineage unmistakable.",
