    blindfoldURL = "Near 1950 in a sealed room overlooking Jaffa’s port, Fomórach Embraces Yusuf bin Yafa while unrest and refugee movement continue below. Yusuf actively seizes Fomórach’s arm and meets his gaze rather than appearing helpless. The first Nosferatu transformation is restrained by shadow. Maps, keys, harbor lights, and guarded streets suggest that this childe’s future loyalty will be political and contested.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Fomórach-24, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/fomorach.webp` as the exact identity reference for Fomórach, subject to the mortal/Embrace instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Pre-Embrace Yusuf bin Yafa.webp` as Yusuf’s exact mortal identity reference and `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Yusuf 'Palis' bin Yafa.webp` as Palis’s exact post-Embrace identity reference; use the appropriate version in each quad, preserving his face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1945–1951, Jaffa, Israel. Fomórach is a Nosferatu vampire throughout this period: preserve the reference identity, severe deformity, powerful frame, and apparently starved, predatory physicality across all four quads. Adapt architecture, clothing, tools, transport, weapons, and infrastructure to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Fomórach is an overlooked listener, survivor, ferocious protector, and infrastructure-minded intelligence gatherer. Show him actively eavesdropping, directing, tunneling, rescuing, hunting, confronting, or making a disastrous choice—not passively posing. Obfuscate and supernatural stealth should read through swallowed light, impossible shadow, or figures overlooking him rather than colorful invisibility effects. Hunger may appear through gaunt tension, frost-like breath, sharpened fangs, and restrained blood-red eye or mouth accents, never glamourized feeding.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, listening-wall viewpoints, or foreground obstructions where they strengthen secrecy, confinement, hunger, or sudden violence. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, monster pin-up posing, or modern horror clichés. Treat famine, colonial violence, war, homelessness, and displacement with gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable documents, logos, extra borders, watermarks, modern anachronisms, or graphic gore.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nDuring fighting around Jaffa, Fomórach moves through a damaged port street carrying medical supplies rather than weapons while Palestinian civilians, Jewish fighters, sailors, and aid workers cross conflicting lines. He points a field medic toward a cellar shelter as gunfire drives others into abandoned homes. Keep the old port recognizable and the communities active; avoid reducing the Nakba to scenery.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a crowded clinic or refugee shelter, Yusuf bin Yafa—later called Palis—organizes water, names, and routes for displaced families while military officials attempt to confiscate supplies. Fomórach watches as Yusuf blocks the doorway and redirects people through a rear courtyard. The moment should explain why resilience, influence, and refusal attract Fomórach’s attention.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nAt night among confiscated homes, Yusuf bin Yafa confronts Fomórach over his true purpose. Yusuf holds a key ring and list without readable text; Fomórach reveals enough of his monstrous face to end deception while pointing toward approaching patrol lights. Their negotiation occurs across a broken threshold, making loyalty, dispossession, and the ethics of offered power visible.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nNear 1950 in a sealed room overlooking Jaffa’s port, Fomórach Embraces Yusuf bin Yafa while unrest and refugee movement continue below. Yusuf actively seizes Fomórach’s arm and meets his gaze rather than appearing helpless. The first Nosferatu transformation is restrained by shadow. Maps, keys, harbor lights, and guarded streets suggest that this childe’s future loyalty will be political and contested.",
