    blindfoldURL = "At a caravan yard near the end of his mortal life, Laleh bint Saif intercepts Rashid after he has exposed a spy hidden among arriving envoys. She stands in traveler’s shadow and offers him a coded object rather than open recruitment; Rashid turns it over while watching the officials he has just manipulated. The moment should make his usefulness to the hidden Web of Knives immediately legible.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-1, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Laleh bint Saif.webp` as exact identity reference for Laleh bint Saif; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1774–1811, Diriyah in the First Saudi State. Rashid is mortal throughout this period: derive a recognizable younger identity from the reference, allow natural aging, and do not give him vampiric pallor, fangs, or the blackened ring before his Embrace. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn a palm-shaded courtyard at night, young mortal Rashid participates in a private Sufi study circle while reformist patrols pass beyond the wall. He quietly shifts sacred books and devotional objects out of sight before opening the gate, then answers a suspicious visitor with controlled courtesy. Mud brick, wells, family rooms, oil lamps, and oasis gardens establish faith practiced under growing ideological pressure.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn Diriyah’s expanding souq, adult Rashid catches a caravan official falsifying weights and redirects grain toward a family quarter while merchants, jurists, soldiers, and tribal envoys argue around him. He listens to three conversations at once and hands different instructions to each side. Use an elevated awning viewpoint to show the oasis capital becoming a state through ordinary administration and compromise.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nInside a formal study hall, Rashid debates Wahhabi reformers and Sufi elders over doctrine, violence, and legitimacy as military recruiters wait at the doorway. He places a travel report between them and points to the human cost of a proposed campaign. The scene should show sincere conviction, political involvement, and moral compromise rather than a simple hero-versus-fanatic divide.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt a caravan yard near the end of his mortal life, Laleh bint Saif intercepts Rashid after he has exposed a spy hidden among arriving envoys. She stands in traveler’s shadow and offers him a coded object rather than open recruitment; Rashid turns it over while watching the officials he has just manipulated. The moment should make his usefulness to the hidden Web of Knives immediately legible.",
