    blindfoldURL = "At an occupation checkpoint outside the ruined city, Rashid bargains for prisoners’ release while secretly preparing departure for Alamut. He trades intelligence and weapons across a rough table, points survivors toward a concealed caravan, and hides the ring beneath a bandaged blackening finger. Laleh bint Saif watches silently from among the rescued, already emotionally unreachable.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-6, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Ibrahim Kethüda.webp`, `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Laleh bint Saif.webp` as exact identity references for Ibrahim Kethüda, Laleh bint Saif; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/composition/rashid-containing-catastrophe-panel-reference.png` only as a composition reference; do not copy its exact setting, figures, or props.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1818, fallen Diriyah. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt the edge of dawn in a shattered palace room, Rashid has staked Prince Ibrahim Kethüda and drags open the shutters that will expose him to sunlight. Ibrahim reaches toward sealed treaties and alliance tokens scattered across the floor; Rashid seizes the prince’s ring and turns away, convinced he has won. Keep the Final Death mostly in blinding architectural light, with triumph already shadowed by consequences.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nDays later, use a high view from a broken watchtower as Rashid races through burning Diriyah and tries to direct civilians away from bombardment and collapsing mud-brick streets. Occupation forces, stripped palm groves, prison lines, looters, and burial parties reveal that Kethüda’s dead agreements had held catastrophe back. Rashid’s commands cannot contain the scale, and the stolen ring glows faintly red in his ash-covered hand.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nAmong the ashes, Laleh bint Saif kneels beside the dead and takes her vow of silence. Rashid reaches toward her with explanations while she raises one hand to stop him and closes her bloodied lips forever. The ring lies between them beside broken household objects and clan messages. Keep them several paces apart; grief, accusation, and the birth of the Piece-Taker’s isolationism should dominate.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt an occupation checkpoint outside the ruined city, Rashid bargains for prisoners’ release while secretly preparing departure for Alamut. He trades intelligence and weapons across a rough table, points survivors toward a concealed caravan, and hides the ring beneath a bandaged blackening finger. Laleh bint Saif watches silently from among the rescued, already emotionally unreachable.",
