    blindfoldURL = "In 1839 at Alamut’s guarded mountain gate, Rashid returns clan insignia to an official and leaves with books, travel gear, and a Constantinople route map without readable text. Messengers arrive behind him with new orders; he closes the gate between himself and the institution. Frame through the portcullis so bars and open mountain road embody disillusionment and chosen departure.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-7, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1819–1839, Alamut, Afghanistan. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn Alamut’s judgment hall, Rashid confesses the destruction of Diriyah before severe Banu Haqim judges. The ring lies visible on his blackened finger as he places Ibrahim Kethüda’s broken alliance tokens on the floor and refuses to minimize the result. Warriors, scribes, prisoners, and servants observe from ordered tiers; use a low viewpoint from beside the evidence to make responsibility, not humiliation, central.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nDeep in the mountain library, Rashid works through clan law, Ur-Shulgi fragments, and accounts of Michael’s Dream while a censor reaches to remove one manuscript. Rashid traps the page beneath his ringed hand and demands the source register. Shelves, lamps, stone passages, scribes, and guarded doors create a world where scholarship itself is politically controlled.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a windswept training yard, Rashid is ordered to execute a defeated prisoner during a martial lesson. Instead, he disarms the supervising warrior’s argument by demonstrating the prisoner’s information value and redirects the exercise into interrogation. Snowy peaks, stone walls, servants’ routes, and watching clan factions make his emerging philosophy a practiced discipline rather than abstract remorse.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn 1839 at Alamut’s guarded mountain gate, Rashid returns clan insignia to an official and leaves with books, travel gear, and a Constantinople route map without readable text. Messengers arrive behind him with new orders; he closes the gate between himself and the institution. Frame through the portcullis so bars and open mountain road embody disillusionment and chosen departure.",
