    blindfoldURL = "During a major urban fire late in the century, Rashid and Sofia Mavridi coordinate rescue and intelligence from a telegraph office. Rashid decodes an intercepted message while Sofia points firefighters toward a threatened archive and servants carry books into the street. Flames provide restrained red accents; telegraph wires, gaslit avenues, steam ferries, and mixed neighborhoods show the city modernizing around their shared project.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-9, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Sofia Mavridi.webp` as exact identity reference for Sofia Mavridi; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1839–1893, Constantinople in the Ottoman Empire. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn a manuscript shop near the Bosphorus, Rashid first meets Sofia Mavridi while both reach for the same damaged account of Michael’s Dream. Sofia pulls the book free and challenges his interpretation; Rashid points toward architectural evidence visible through the window. Scholars, servants, clergy, diplomats, and street traffic frame an intellectual collision that becomes partnership rather than romance posing.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn their expanding Nephilim library, Rashid and Sofia Mavridi direct servants and scribes during a sudden police search. Sofia hides censored texts behind a false shelf while Rashid calmly presents reform-era permits and reroutes one investigator toward harmless records. Wooden quarters, maps, icons, Islamic manuscripts, archaeological fragments, and Bosphorus light show a household built for research and coexistence.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nDuring Tanzimat-era debate in a ministry salon, Rashid and Sofia Mavridi stand on opposite sides of a table crowded with jurists, Sufis, diplomats, artists, and Kindred. Rashid adjusts a proposed legal compromise while Sofia physically moves rival delegates into conversation. Gaslight, European and Ottoman dress, reform papers without readable text, and guarded doors make governance experimentation active and contested.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nDuring a major urban fire late in the century, Rashid and Sofia Mavridi coordinate rescue and intelligence from a telegraph office. Rashid decodes an intercepted message while Sofia points firefighters toward a threatened archive and servants carry books into the street. Flames provide restrained red accents; telegraph wires, gaslit avenues, steam ferries, and mixed neighborhoods show the city modernizing around their shared project.",
