    blindfoldURL = "At the mountain gate in 1901, Rashid departs with copied rites hidden among ordinary scholarly trunks while an official demands one final oath. He returns a ceremonial blade but keeps the blackened ring visible, then signals waiting couriers toward Constantinople. Dawn colors stay cold and monochrome; one deep-red glow inside the luggage hints at the dangerous knowledge he carries back to Sofia.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-12, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1893–1901, Alamut, Afghanistan. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nRashid returns to Alamut after half a century and is searched at the gate by younger warriors who treat him as a renegade. He places Sofia’s sealed blood sample and his blackened ring on the inspection table but refuses to surrender either. Snow, pack animals, telegram cases, old stone, and modernized rifles emphasize strained dependence on an institution he despises.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nIn a deep ritual library, Rashid studies ancestral-memory rites with sorcerers who deliberately withhold a crucial page. He catches the omission when red calligraphic geometry fails to close, then locks the chamber until they bargain honestly. Manuscripts remain unreadable; the action should show technical mastery, political pressure, and the cost of acquiring forbidden knowledge.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a circular testing chamber, a rival forces Rashid to contain several collapsing blood-memory reflections at once. Rashid plants his ringed hand against the floor and draws the red structures into one coherent threshold while judges watch from balconies. Use a high angle that keeps the contained images legible but subordinate to Rashid’s disciplined control—no purple smoke or generic energy beams.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAt the mountain gate in 1901, Rashid departs with copied rites hidden among ordinary scholarly trunks while an official demands one final oath. He returns a ceremonial blade but keeps the blackened ring visible, then signals waiting couriers toward Constantinople. Dawn colors stay cold and monochrome; one deep-red glow inside the luggage hints at the dangerous knowledge he carries back to Sofia.",
