    blindfoldURL = "Under Allied occupation, Rashid discovers Laleh’s trail has vanished from a wall of Nephilim, Ottoman, and clan correspondence. Sofia Mavridi points toward one final European route while foreign soldiers search the street below. Rashid closes the ritual chamber, takes the blackened ring and travel papers, and steps toward departure. The moment should begin the long search without depicting Laleh physically.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-13, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Sofia Mavridi.webp`, `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Michael the Archangel.webp` as exact identity references for Sofia Mavridi, Michael the Archangel; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/composition/rashid-containing-catastrophe-panel-reference.png` only as a composition reference; do not copy its exact setting, figures, or props.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1901–1922, Constantinople in the Ottoman Empire. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nIn the Nephilim ritual chamber, Rashid and Sofia Mavridi enter an ancestral blood memory together. They brace opposite sides of a deep-red circular threshold whose interior reveals a coherent, monochrome reflection of Michael the Archangel—not a physical visitor—standing amid ancient Constantinople. The reflection addresses them while library objects lift in the pressure. Keep Michael awe-inspiring but partially defined by light and memory rather than literal fantasy spectacle.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nAs Michael the Archangel’s reflection reveals Ur-Shulgi’s destructive truth and prophecy, Rashid tries to contain the memory while Sofia Mavridi reaches toward a collapsing ancestral image. The stolen ring fuses to Rashid’s hand, blackening his finger and blazing deep red. Use a dramatic low angle from the ring’s level; Michael remains inside the memory threshold, and the catastrophe is held by Rashid’s disciplined geometry rather than exploding across the whole room.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nDuring World War I, Rashid and Sofia Mavridi run a relief and intelligence operation from their library while refugees, couriers, and wounded soldiers crowd the halls. Rashid catches a censored telegram, redirects food toward a threatened district, and seals occult records before military police enter. Sofia organizes evacuees at another doorway. Telephones, electric trams, uniforms, and blackout curtains place sorcery inside practical wartime responsibility.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nUnder Allied occupation, Rashid discovers Laleh’s trail has vanished from a wall of Nephilim, Ottoman, and clan correspondence. Sofia Mavridi points toward one final European route while foreign soldiers search the street below. Rashid closes the ritual chamber, takes the blackened ring and travel papers, and steps toward departure. The moment should begin the long search without depicting Laleh physically.",
