    blindfoldURL = "In the 1990s, Rashid and Laleh bint Saif examine contradictory Red List dossiers tied to Kemintiri without depicting her as any confirmed identity. Rashid pins false seals beneath red light while Laleh silently identifies the one pattern shared across the files. Visitors wait behind security glass and Toronto towers rise outside, showing institutional corruption turning sheltered scholarship into purpose.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-21, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/npcs/Laleh bint Saif.webp` as exact identity reference for Laleh bint Saif; preserve each named figure’s face, apparent age, build, and distinguishing features while adapting costume and grooming to the period.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 1952–1997, Toronto, Canada. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nAt Union Station in the early 1950s, Rashid follows the Atlantic lead through winter crowds and identifies Laleh bint Saif at a distance by an old silent hand signal. She does not approach; Rashid uses a restrained ancestral-memory reflection in the station glass to confirm her identity while travelers pass between them. The scene should make reunion cautious, public, and nearly impossible after more than a century.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nInside Laleh bint Saif’s concealed Toronto haven, Rashid faces his sire across a bare judgment table. She remains bound by her vow of silence and places objects from Diriyah between them; Rashid exposes the blackened ring and answers her gestures. Martial tools, ritual chambers, immigrant-street light, and guarded doors make the first audience both shelter and reckoning, with no embrace or sentimental posing.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nDuring the 1970s or 1980s, Rashid and Laleh bint Saif conduct a disciplined training and research session while Toronto modernizes outside. She attacks a flaw in his stance; he redirects the lesson toward a map of Ur-Shulgi references and Camarilla contacts. Fax machines, early computers, security monitors, industrial waterfront views, and immigrant community records show old clan refuge becoming an intelligence center.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nIn the 1990s, Rashid and Laleh bint Saif examine contradictory Red List dossiers tied to Kemintiri without depicting her as any confirmed identity. Rashid pins false seals beneath red light while Laleh silently identifies the one pattern shared across the files. Visitors wait behind security glass and Toronto towers rise outside, showing institutional corruption turning sheltered scholarship into purpose.",
