    blindfoldURL = "After the Odense Pact is agreed, Rashid stands in a quiet rail-station or university courtyard coordinating the immediate consequences: escorts for vulnerable delegates, secure copies, emergency calls, and routes home. Other negotiators shake hands in the background while he notices one missing observer and closes a red-lit file. The final concept should feel like order constructed through exhausting practical work, not a ceremonial victory portrait.",
    splashText = "COMMON INSTRUCTIONS\nCreate one textless 1920x1080 concept-sampler image for Rashid-26, divided into four equal 16:9 quads in a clean 2x2 grid: Quad A top-left, Quad B top-right, Quad C bottom-left, and Quad D bottom-right. Each quad must occupy exactly one quarter of the canvas and depict a different unified frozen moment suitable for later expansion into a full 1920x1080 Memoriam splash. Use a narrow neutral-black cross-shaped gutter; do not let figures, architecture, smoke, weather, or lighting cross between quads.\n\nREFERENCE INPUTS — Attach these files as actual image inputs. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/combined/memoriam-splash-style-contact-sheet.png` only as the rendering and composition guide: cinematic gothic-noir realism, near-monochrome black, charcoal, and cold silver, hard contrast, deep negative space, wet or metallic highlights, layered atmospheric depth, and restrained blood-red accents. Do not copy its characters, Toronto locations, symbols, readable words, or exact compositions. Attach `assets/input/character-intro-splashes/characters/rashid.webp` as the exact identity reference for Rashid Abdulrahman, subject to the mortal instruction below.\n\nCHARACTER AND PERIOD — Set all concepts within 2013, Odense, Denmark. Rashid is an ageless Banu Haqim vampire throughout this period: preserve the same apparent age and identity across all four quads. After 1818, Ur-Shulgi’s Promise is permanently bound to his hand as a blackened ring and finger that may glow restrained deep red under supernatural pressure. Adapt architecture, clothing, weapons, manuscripts, transport, institutions, and religious practice to the exact decade and geography of each quad. Rashid is a disciplined spy, scholar, mediator, occultist, and administrator haunted by the consequences of decisive action. Show him actively observing, debating, containing, negotiating, researching, rescuing, or choosing—not passively posing. Blood Sorcery appears as restrained geometric skeins, calligraphic structures without readable words, or seals of deep-red light. Ancestral memory may appear as a coherent reflection within a red-black threshold, not Chimerstry’s purple smoke and not generic fantasy beams.\n\nCAMERA AND STYLE — Keep the chronicle’s primary high-contrast black-and-white gothic-noir language with selective deep-red accents. Use mostly clear cinematic framing, with one or two purposeful low angles, high angles, restrained Dutch tilts, over-the-shoulder viewpoints, or architectural foreground obstructions where they strengthen surveillance, judgment, responsibility, or catastrophe. Avoid fisheye distortion, broken anatomy, static lineups, superhero posing, generic desert fantasy, or Orientalist ornament. Treat Sufi and Islamic practice, political violence, occupation, war, and displacement with historical gravity. Reserve a calm, dark, low-detail area inside every quad for later overlays. No montage within a quad, captions, labels, readable manuscripts, logos, extra borders, watermarks, or anachronisms.\n\nQUAD A — TOP LEFT\nRashid arrives at a restrained contemporary Odense hotel conference venue during rain and immediately spots that rival security teams have duplicated credentials. He calmly separates delegates into two entrances while interpreters, lawyers, academics, drivers, and young vampires react. Historic streets, bicycles, rail connections, modern glass, and muted Danish interiors establish an international gathering without spectacle.\n\nQUAD B — TOP RIGHT\nAt the central negotiation table, Rashid stands between Schismatic Banu Haqim delegates and Camarilla representatives as both sides reach for incompatible draft terms. He physically rotates the documents toward a shared clause, removes a ceremonial weapon from the table, and forces attention back to governance. Use a low angle from table level; deep-red accents are limited to his ring and security indicators.\n\nQUAD C — BOTTOM LEFT\nIn a hotel corridor during a recess, Rashid catches an unnamed young fledgling observer using contradictory credentials—an ambiguous possible Kemintiri identity, never confirmed. Rather than attack, he redirects security, closes one exit, and asks a precise question while the figure’s face remains partly obscured. The scene should communicate institutional uncertainty and vigilance without declaring that Kemintiri was canonically present.\n\nQUAD D — BOTTOM RIGHT\nAfter the Odense Pact is agreed, Rashid stands in a quiet rail-station or university courtyard coordinating the immediate consequences: escorts for vulnerable delegates, secure copies, emergency calls, and routes home. Other negotiators shake hands in the background while he notices one missing observer and closes a red-lit file. The final concept should feel like order constructed through exhausting practical work, not a ceremonial victory portrait.",
